<title>PERU: Peru net reserves rise to $8.482 bln Sept 30.</title>
<headline>Peru net reserves rise to $8.482 bln Sept 30.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Central Reserve Bank said Friday its net international reserves stood at $8.423 billion on September 30, up from $8.423 billion the week before.</p>
<p>The bank's foreign exchange position, or total liquidity minus short and long-term debt obligations, was $1.690 billion on the same day.</p>
<p>International reserves ended 1995 at $6.641 billion.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
